{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2290 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "9cfbc48b4ddc9da7f4d3823aac855079e314c421170f8c543dd35c0ccfa31780" :edb/db-before-t 2289 :edb/db-after-t 2290 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535602 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:23:10.346Z" 13194139535602 true] [17592186357000 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357001 13194139535602 false] [17592186357000 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357021 13194139535602 true] [17592186357000 1100 "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=xy+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z$ that passes through the point $P(0,1,1).$" 13194139535602 false] [17592186357000 1100 "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=xy+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z$ that passes through the point $P(0,1,1).$\n\nGive the full level set, including the necessary range restriction from the principal real arcsine.\n\nHint: Compute $f(0,1,1)$, then use the principal range $-\\pi/2\\le\\arcsin z\\le\\pi/2$ before taking sine." 13194139535602 true] [17592186357000 1145 "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,1,1) & =0\\cdot 1+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ xy+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z & =\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-xy \\\\ z & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-xy) \\\\ z & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(0,1,1)$ is the surface $z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy.$" 13194139535602 false] [17592186357000 1145 "The level surface through $P=(0,1,1)$ has level constant\n$$c=f(0,1,1)=0+\\arcsin(1)=\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$$\nThus $xy+\\arcsin z=\\pi/2$, or $\\arcsin z=\\pi/2-xy$. The principal real arcsine takes values in $[-\\pi/2,\\pi/2]$. Therefore\n$$-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\frac{\\pi}{2}-xy\\le\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad 0\\le xy\\le\\pi.$$\nTaking sine gives $z=\\sin(\\pi/2-xy)=\\cos(xy)$. Conversely, if $0\\le xy\\le\\pi$ and $z=\\cos(xy)$, then $\\pi/2-xy$ lies in the principal arcsine range, so $\\arcsin z=\\pi/2-xy$ and $f(x,y,z)=\\pi/2$. The exact full level set is\n$$\\boxed{\\{(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3:z=\\cos(xy),\\ 0\\le xy\\le\\pi\\}}.$$\nThe range restriction is essential. For instance $(x,y,z)=(2\\pi,1,1)$ satisfies $z=\\cos(xy)$, but $f(2\\pi,1,1)=2\\pi+\\pi/2=5\\pi/2$, not $\\pi/2$. The source's revealed answer a provides the algebraic relation but omits the restriction. Its original prompt, options, source grade and solution remain preserved; the study choice supplies the complete level set without changing the original function or point." 13194139535602 true] [17592186357021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357002 13194139535602 true] [17592186357021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357003 13194139535602 true] [17592186357021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357004 13194139535602 true] [17592186357021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357005 13194139535602 true] [17592186357021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357006 13194139535602 true] [17592186357021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357022 13194139535602 true] [17592186357021 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535602 true] [17592186357021 1041 "selection" 13194139535602 true] [17592186357021 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357022 13194139535602 true] [17592186357021 1110 #uuid "6ce0ae16-eae7-50e8-8ea5-58dac8da8c7f" 13194139535602 true] [17592186357022 1034 "z=\\cos(xy),\\quad 0\\le xy\\le\\pi" 13194139535602 true] [17592186357022 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535602 true] [17592186357022 1111 #uuid "edbdadbd-4697-59bf-985c-9065cd719ac6" 13194139535602 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-37131/principal-arcsin-exact-level-set-v1/selection" 17592186357021 "q-37131/principal-arcsin-exact-level-set-v1/selection/answer-complete-level-set" 17592186357022}}
